To sum this all up:

If you name a spellbook individually and leave it in a stash, you can't
check the last read time without coming back to the stash to look at that
particular book. 

Non-individually given spellbook names are not shown when you look at it,
only with the \ command. And you don't need to carry the book itself to
check that.

If you want to keep count of how many times you have read one particular
book, that can be done with individual naming. 

So, non-individual naming for the turn counter of last time you read a
spell and individual naming for the read counter of a certain book is a
good combination, if you want to keep track of both numbers.

